# For local overrides: `cp .env.example .env.local`, then turn on only the values you need (.env.local is not committed).

# The API origin to connect to. Unset, both the dev server and local builds use http://localhost:3001.
# The code attaches the path prefix (/v2); write only the origin here.
#
# Deployment images bake in that deployment's API origin as a build argument (apps/web/Dockerfile). This
# file is local-only, so it never defaults to a production domain: `pnpm dev` must not quietly touch
# any production data.
#
# Turn on only when you want to point local at a deployed API.
# VITE_API_ORIGIN=https://api-staging.example.com

# The origin of the operations console (apps/admin): where the account screen's `Operations tools` link points.
# Unset, the dev server uses http://localhost:3002 (the port `pnpm dev:admin` serves on).
#
# **Production builds have no default**: when empty, that link section is not drawn.
# Why it does not fall back to a guessed domain is in the src/lib/admin-console.ts header.
#
# Turn on only when you want to point at a deployed console locally.
# VITE_ADMIN_ORIGIN=https://admin.example.com
